# Project standards (AI / contributors)

## Language

- **Code**: identifiers, function names, and file names in English.
- **Comments**: all comments and JSDoc in **English** (inline, block, and file headers) so tooling and models parse intent reliably.
- **User communication**: when the user writes in **Portuguese (PT-BR)**, reply in **Portuguese (PT-BR)**; otherwise match the user’s language.

## Scripts and modules

- Prefer **ES modules** (`.mjs`) for Node utilities in this repo.
- Prefer `const` over `let`; avoid `var`.
- Use descriptive names; avoid single-letter identifiers except in trivial loop indices.

## Changelog-style discipline (when editing release notes)

- Keep **changelog narrative compact**; avoid pasting huge file lists into narrative changelog text.
- When listing **which files** changed per release, use a dedicated list or release-notes file pattern if the project adds one later.

## Data hygiene (`data/$themes.json`)

- Figma binding payloads (`$figmaStyleReferences`, `figmaVariableReferences`, `$figmaVariableReferences`) should stay **empty objects** for sample/template repos unless you intentionally re-link to a Figma file.
- Use `npm run themes:clean-figma` (or `node utils/clean-themes-figma-references.mjs`) after exports that reintroduce those IDs.
